{"base_rate":0.46367851622874806,"brier":0.3561752704791345,"bss":-0.43225911431316044,"bss_hi":-0.30139256962710875,"bss_lo":-0.5985195528826698,"chart":{"base":[663.2,103.4],"fp":[302.0,197.9],"lead":"62,258.2 272,253 482,254.3 692,233.9","note":{"base":"skill -0.43 — higher than 4% of cities","fp":"low end +10pp, high end +39pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 62% of cities","rel":"promised 24% → rained 32%; promised 98% → rained 55%"},"rel":"214.3,326.4 455.4,278.5 597.9,264.2 680.3,230.5"},"country":"CO","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.3059659969088099,"ess":463.08898480263264,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Bogota</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Bogota rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>56%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(12%), there is still roughly a <b>21%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 647 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 12.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.43, ranked 204 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(202&ndash;208) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>62</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'><b>43%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>54%</td><td class='num'><b>45%</b></td><td class='num'>60</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>70%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>60</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>52%</b></td><td class='num'>62</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>50%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>194</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Bogota</b> <span class=\"muted\">Colombia</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>-0.43</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>202&ndash;208\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>647 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Bogota &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Bogota\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"100.99387096774194,305.6774193548387 182.3685294117647,216.05882352941177 249.51399999999998,139.33333333333334 304.7226086956522,91.85507246376812 347.1,48.33333333333337 370.7761290322581,35.61290322580646 391.2025,23.055555555555543 410.6861855670103,18.0 410.6861855670103,23.62886597938143 391.2025,63.5 370.7761290322581,88.45161290322585 347.1,121.13333333333333 304.7226086956522,165.71014492753625 249.51399999999998,230.33333333333331 182.3685294117647,296.3529411764706 100.99387096774194,364.38709677419354\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"213.2210200927357\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"213.2210200927357\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"100.99387096774194,305.6774193548387 182.3685294117647,226.76470588235296 249.51399999999998,218.2 304.7226086956522,229.0144927536232 347.1,230.33333333333331 370.7761290322581,194.1290322580645 391.2025,200.0 410.6861855670103,177.48453608247422\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 12%&amp;#10;It rained 21% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 62 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"100.99387096774194\" cy=\"305.6774193548387\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 35%&amp;#10;It rained 43% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"182.3685294117647\" cy=\"226.76470588235296\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 54%&amp;#10;It rained 45% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 60 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"249.51399999999998\" cy=\"218.2\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 70%&amp;#10;It rained 42% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"304.7226086956522\" cy=\"229.0144927536232\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 42% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 60 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"347.1\" cy=\"230.33333333333331\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 52% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 62 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"370.7761290322581\" cy=\"194.1290322580645\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 94%&amp;#10;It rained 50% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"391.2025\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 56% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 194 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.6861855670103\" cy=\"177.48453608247422\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(46%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Bogota the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (-0.26) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.66).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>172</td><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'>-0.665</td><td class='num'>39.3%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>165</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>-0.569</td><td class='num'>32.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'>-0.467</td><td class='num'>31.2%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>136</td><td class='num'>63%</td><td class='num'>-0.265</td><td class='num'>25.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":4.60971,"lon":-74.08175,"n":647,"n_cities":213,"name":"Bogota","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.25,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.1214516129032258,"n":62,"obs":0.20967741935483872,"sig":false},{"hi":0.4520000000000002,"lo":0.25,"mean":0.3513235294117647,"n":68,"obs":0.4264705882352941,"sig":false},{"hi":0.63,"lo":0.4520000000000002,"mean":0.5409999999999999,"n":60,"obs":0.45,"sig":false},{"hi":0.7680000000000007,"lo":0.63,"mean":0.6969565217391304,"n":69,"obs":0.42028985507246375,"sig":true},{"hi":0.86,"lo":0.7680000000000007,"mean":0.8166666666666667,"n":60,"obs":0.4166666666666667,"sig":true},{"hi":0.92,"lo":0.86,"mean":0.8835483870967743,"n":62,"obs":0.5161290322580645,"sig":true},{"hi":0.9720000000000004,"lo":0.92,"mean":0.9412499999999999,"n":72,"obs":0.5,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9720000000000004,"mean":0.9962886597938144,"n":194,"obs":0.5618556701030928,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":12.5,"provisional":false,"rank":204,"rank_hi":208.0,"rank_lo":202.0,"reliability":0.11630194910804491,"resolution":0.010051573692542977,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"bogota","station":"","timezone":"America/Bogota"}